en_US:
In the Global Terminal, you can battle or
trade Pokémon with Pokémon fans from{VAR BE00}
around the world by connecting to{VAR BE00}
Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection.{VAR BE01}
For details, please listen to the
explanation at each facility.{VAR BE01}

You may trade Pokémon with other
Pokémon fans from around the world with{VAR BE00}
Global Trade.{VAR BE01}
Global Trade has two forms: GTS and
GTS Negotiations.{VAR BE01}
Please be careful, because each has a
different way of trading.{VAR BE01}

You may trade Pokémon in two ways when
using GTS.{VAR BE01}
You may offer a Pokémon for trade
or search among offered Pokémon.{VAR BE01}

You will be asked to put up the
Pokémon you are offering to trade.{VAR BE01}
At that time, you will be asked what
Pokémon you would like in return.{VAR BE01}
If another player offers your desired
Pokémon in return for your offered{VAR BE00}
Pokémon, the trade will go through.{VAR BE01}

You may search among the Pokémon
that are offered by other Trainers.{VAR BE01}
They will all identify what Pokémon
their Trainers want back in return.{VAR BE01}
If you find one that you want, you
must provide us with the kind of{VAR BE00}
Pokémon wanted in return.{VAR BE01}

In GTS Negotiations, you set the trading
conditions based on what kinds of{VAR BE00}
Pokémon you'd like to trade.{VAR BE01}
If you find a person with matching
conditions, you may proceed to a{VAR BE00}
Negotiation Trade with that person.{VAR BE01}
In order to trade, you need to have two
or more Pokémon in your party.{VAR BE01}

In a Negotiation Trade, each person
offers three Pokémon to trade.{VAR BE01}
Then, each person will choose one of the
other person's three Pokémon.{VAR BE01}

You can set three conditions in a
Negotiation Trade: the level of Pokémon{VAR BE00}
to trade, the Pokémon you want to{VAR BE00}
receive, and the Pokémon up for offer.{VAR BE01}
You may trade with a person whose
conditions match yours, or choose{VAR BE00}
Trade Rendezvous to try another trade{VAR BE00}
with a previous trading partner.{VAR BE01}

With Battle Videos, you may post a
Battle Video you took with your{VAR BE00}
Vs. Recorder or view Battle Videos from{VAR BE00}
other Trainers.{VAR BE01}
You may search the Battle Videos by
Pokémon, battle facility, ranking, etc.{VAR BE01}
The Battle Video you post will be assigned
a 12-digit code.{VAR BE01}
Your friends may view your Battle Video
by entering this 12-digit code here.{VAR BE01}

With Musical Photos, you may post a photo
you took at the Pokémon Musical in{VAR BE00}
Nimbasa City by using the Vs. Recorder.{VAR BE01}
You may also view photos taken by other
people, sorted by the Pokémon you like.{VAR BE01}

A Random Matchup is a battle with other
Pokémon fans from around the world.{VAR BE01}
There are five kinds of Random Matchups:
Single, Double, Triple, Rotation,{VAR BE00}
and Launcher.{VAR BE01}
Also, Random Matchups have two modes:
Free mode and Rating mode.{VAR BE01}
In Free mode, everyone can participate
in battles freely.{VAR BE01}
In Rating mode, you may participate in
battles after you set Game Sync, access{VAR BE00}
the Pokémon Global Link website with your{VAR BE00}
computer, and register your{VAR BE00}
Game Sync ID.{VAR BE01}
http://www.pokemon-gl.com/
(Pokémon Global Link){VAR BE01}

Free mode is for casual battles against
other Pokémon fans around the world.{VAR BE01}
Feel free to challenge it!{VAR BE01}

Rating mode is recommended for those who
want to master battles.{VAR BE01}
When communication is established, you
are likely to battle against a person with{VAR BE00}
a similar Rating.{VAR BE01}
Your Rating starts at 1500. When you win,
it goes up. When you lose, it goes down.{VAR BE01}
So the higher your Rating is, the
stronger you are as a Trainer!{VAR BE01}
There's one thing you should be careful
about in Rating mode.{VAR BE01}
Your record and Rating will be erased if
you connect to Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection{VAR BE00}
with a different DS System.{VAR BE01}
So please be careful if you switch!{VAR BE01}

There are several special rules
for Random Matchups.{VAR BE01}
Any Pokémon higher than Lv. 50 will be
set to that level for the battle.{VAR BE01}
Pokémon nicknames won't be used.{VAR BE01}
You have a limited time to choose Pokémon
for a battle and to give orders to your{VAR BE00}
Pokémon during the battle.{VAR BE01}
Don't exceed the time limit,
or your Pokémon and its moves{VAR BE00}
will be chosen for you!{VAR BE01}
There's also a time limit on the battle.{VAR BE01}
The winner will be determined when time
runs out, even if both sides still have{VAR BE00}
Pokémon standing.{VAR BE01}

For a Single Battle, you need to have
three to six Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
Before a battle, you and your opponent
show your Pokémon to each other,{VAR BE00}
then choose three Pokémon and battle.{VAR BE01}
You may not have duplicate Pokémon
or held items.{VAR BE01}
Also, you can't take special Pokémon
or Eggs into battle.{VAR BE01}

For a Double Battle, you need to have
four to six Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
Before a battle, you and your opponent
show your Pokémon to each other,{VAR BE00}
then choose four Pokémon and battle.{VAR BE01}
You may not have duplicate Pokémon
or held items.{VAR BE01}
Also, you can't take special Pokémon
or Eggs into battle.{VAR BE01}

For a Triple Battle, you need to have
six Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
Before a battle, you and your opponent
show your Pokémon to each other,{VAR BE00}
then decide their order and battle.{VAR BE01}
You may not have duplicate Pokémon
or held items.{VAR BE01}
Also, you can't take special Pokémon
or Eggs into battle.{VAR BE01}

In a Rotation Battle, you need to have
four to six Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
Before a battle, you and your opponent
show your Pokémon to each other,{VAR BE00}
then choose four Pokémon and battle.{VAR BE01}
You may not have duplicate Pokémon
or held items.{VAR BE01}
Also, you can't take special Pokémon
or Eggs into battle.{VAR BE01}

In a Launcher Battle, you have a
Triple Battle with your Wonder Launcher.{VAR BE00}
You need to have six Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
Before a battle, you and your opponent
show your Pokémon to each other,{VAR BE00}
then decide their order and battle.{VAR BE01}
You may not have duplicate Pokémon
or held items.{VAR BE01}
Also, you can't take special Pokémon
or Eggs into battle.{VAR BE01}

